Public API: heat_balance::ctf_initial_owner::initialize_construction_ctf_initial
accepts the actual Construction, actual prior construction-vector prefix, actual
used construction IDs (BTreeSet<u32>), the same preprocessing result/context,
and the actual caller timestep. It returns ConstructionCtfInitialDiscretization:
construction_id, context, time_step_zone_hours, and result. The result is the
accepted CtfInitialDiscretization or an explicit CtfInitialUnavailable route:
PreprocessingScope, UnusedConstruction, PreprocessingErrorReturn,
PostConversionUnavailable, AllResistiveBranch, ReverseConstruction with the
actual earlier construction_id, or InitialScope. External unit observers may
reuse this same owner function; they must not reconstruct reverse classification.

Normal initialization calls existing construction_thermal_data once and passes
its actual CTF01 Result to this ingress. It retains actual opaque owner order,
shared loading ErrorsFound, surface-referenced use, no-source/1D context and the
literal 1.0/f64(timestep_count) caller. Massive dispatch is exactly layers >
num_res_layers; reverse matching uses original MaterialIds and prior use before
the unchanged pure initial phase. No numerical similarity determines a route.
HeatBalanceState.construction_ctf03_initial copies the actual ordered vector.

The existing construction_thermal_data and construction_cache_hash function
bodies are byte-identical. EIO/CTF02 coefficient precedence, surface coefficient
state, cache hash inputs and invalidation semantics are preserved. The new
initial owner is excluded from that historical coefficient hash. Build timing
naturally includes the additional initialization work.

